  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "# Issue:\nOpening the `Action Menu` does not block your interaction with the world. So if you are looking at a Pickup Object for example, then open your `Action Menu` and then click on something like the `Options` page, you will notice that the Pickup Object will still come to your hand.\n**Repro Steps:**\n1. Open VRChat in desktop mode and go to the default home.\n2. Go to the couch area and look at one of the pillows on the ground.\n3. Open your `Action Menu`.\n4. Now just click on the `Options` button.\n- You will notice that now the Pillow will come to your hand, just like if you normally clicked on it.\nThis works with anything you can normally interact with, such as buttons, Avatar Pedestals, etc.\n\n# Expected Behavior:\nIn live you can’t interact with the world once your Action Menu is open, this should also be the case with the new Input System. Currently you can accidentally just grab stuff in worlds or press buttons you didn’t mean to press.\n**Video showcasing the issue:**\nhttps://streamable.com/3y9u31",
